# CoastVision React Native — Production Coding Rules

These rules apply when building or editing the CoastVision Android app (`frontend/mobile/`) and shared client code (`frontend/shared/`).

## 1. Project Structure (Mandatory)

Never put the whole app in one file. Match this layout:

**Do:** one screen per file, reusable hooks, shared API factory.
**Don't:** 2000-line App.js, inline fetch in JSX, duplicated poll logic.

## 2. Layer Separation

| Layer | Responsibility | Must NOT contain |
|-------|----------------|------------------|
| `shared/api.js` | HTTP requests, URL builders | React hooks, UI, AsyncStorage |
| `context/ApiContext.js` | Base URL state, createApi provider | Screen-specific UI |
| `hooks/` | Polling, app lifecycle, derived state | JSX, StyleSheet |
| `screens/` | Compose components, wire hooks | Raw fetch strings |
| `components/` | Display props, emit events | Direct API calls |

All network access goes through `createApi(baseUrl)`. Screens use `useApi()` from context — never hardcode `http://192.168.x.x:8000` outside Settings.

## 3. API Layer Rules

- Single factory `createApi(baseUrl)` in `shared/api.js`
- Normalize baseUrl: trim whitespace, strip trailing `/`
- Every method throws on non-2xx status
- `hlsUrl(zid)` returns a string — it is not a fetch call
- New endpoints are added only in `api.js`, never in screens

## 4. Server URL & Connection

- Persist URL in AsyncStorage under one key: `coastvision_api_url`
- Settings screen: URL input, Test Connection, save, green/red status dot
- Show `ConnectionBanner` on all tabs when backend is unreachable
- Validate `http://` or `https://` before saving
- No hardcoded laptop IPs in screen files

## 5. Screen Conventions

| Screen | File | Key behavior |
|--------|------|--------------|
| Dashboard | `DashboardScreen.js` | FlatList zone cards, HLS, pull-to-refresh |
| Analytics | `AnalyticsScreen.js` | Lazy sub-tabs; charts load on tab focus |
| Event Logs | `EventLogsScreen.js` | Activity events + Respond action |
| Settings | `SettingsScreen.js` | Profile, server URL, health check, sign out |

- 4 bottom tabs via `@react-navigation/bottom-tabs` (Dashboard, Analytics, Logs, Settings)
- Lifeguard accounts managed on **web admin** only — no mobile Lifeguards tab
- Zone detail in separate `ZoneDetailScreen.js` (stack, not inline modal)
- Max ~250 lines per screen — extract into `components/`

## 6. Performance (Battery & Wi-Fi)

- Pause polling when app is backgrounded (`AppState`)
- Pause polling when tab is not focused (`useIsFocused`)
- Lazy-load Analytics — fetch only when user opens that sub-tab
- Poll intervals live in `constants.js`:

| Data | Interval | Scope |
|------|----------|-------|
| Health | 5s | Settings / status |
| Zones | 2s | Dashboard tab only |
| Detections | 1.5s | Visible zone cards only |
| Alerts | 3s | Event Logs tab only |
| Analytics | On focus | No background polling |

- HLS via `react-native-video` only — no parallel MJPEG + frame polling
- Use `FlatList` with `keyExtractor` and `React.memo` on list items
- Cancel requests on unmount (`AbortController` in hooks)

## 7. UI & Components

- Use `react-native-paper` for buttons, cards, inputs, snackbars
- Components are presentational — props in, events out
- `StyleSheet.create` at file bottom or shared `theme.js`
- No magic numbers — use named constants
- Drowning alerts use distinct severity colors from `constants.js`

## 8. Error Handling & UX

- try/catch on all async loads; show `Snackbar`, not stack traces
- `ActivityIndicator` on first load; empty states with helpful text
- Pull-to-refresh on Dashboard and Analytics
- Network error message: "Cannot reach server — check Wi-Fi and URL in Settings"
- Video errors on `ZoneCard` must not crash the list

## 9. Alerts & Notifications

- Centralize in `hooks/useAlertNotifications.js`
- `expo-av` for sound, `expo-haptics` for vibration on drowning alerts
- Track `lastSeenAlertId` to avoid repeat alarms on every poll
- Unread badge on Event Logs tab

## 10. Code Clarity & Naming

- PascalCase: `ZoneCard.js`, `DashboardScreen.js`
- camelCase hooks: `usePollApi.js`
- UPPER_SNAKE constants: `POLL_ZONES_MS`
- verb-first functions: `fetchZones`, `testConnection`
- One default export per file
- Comments only for non-obvious logic (SSE, HLS retry)

## 11. What Not to Do

- Do not copy web `App.jsx` as a mobile monolith
- Do not import from `frontend/web/` — share via `frontend/shared/` only
- Do not store secrets (Telegram bot token) in the mobile app
- Do not poll all endpoints globally at app root
- Do not use `console.log` as the only error path in production code

## 12. New Feature Checklist

1. Endpoint in `shared/api.js`?
2. UI in `components/`, wired in screen?
3. Repeated logic in `hooks/`?
4. Constants in `shared/constants.js`?
5. Server URL from `ApiContext`?
6. 20+ items → `FlatList`, not `ScrollView.map`?
7. Interval fetch → `usePollApi` with focus/AppState?

## 13. Approved Dependencies

expo, react-native, @react-navigation/native, @react-navigation/bottom-tabs,
react-native-video, react-native-chart-kit, react-native-svg,
@react-native-async-storage/async-storage, react-native-paper, expo-av, expo-haptics

Do not add new libraries without a documented reason.

## 14. Refactor Triggers

Stop and refactor when:
- Any screen exceeds 250 lines
- Any component exceeds 150 lines
- The same API path appears in more than one file
- `setInterval` is written outside `usePollApi`